.TH NOTIFYD 1 2026-11-10 "notifyd 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
notifyd \- desktop notification daemon for X11 with rules, presets and a colorful log
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B notifyd daemon
.RB [ \-c
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-renderer
.BR gtk | none ]
.RB [ \-\-replace ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-format
.BR pretty | json ]
.RB [ \-\-color
.BR auto | always | never ]
.RB [ \-v | \-q ]
.br
.B notifyd send
.RI [ options ]
.I summary
.RI [ body ]
.br
.B notifyd ctl
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.br
.B notifyd presets
.RB [ \-\-pick | \-\-names ]
.br
.B notifyd import
.BR deadd " [" \-\-yml
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-css
.IR path ]
|
.BR dunst " [" \-\-rc
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B notifyd check
.RB [ \-c
.IR path ]
.br
.B notifyd rules
.RB [ \-c
.IR path ]
.RI [ fields ]
.br
.B notifyd completion
.BR zsh | bash | fish
.br
.B notifyd help
.RI [ command ...]
.br
.B notifyd version
.RB | " \-V" | " \-\-version"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B notifyd
is a server for the freedesktop.org Desktop Notifications specification (1.2): it owns
.B org.freedesktop.Notifications
on the session bus and draws the notifications applications send as translucent GTK3 popups
on X11. It combines deadd\-notification\-center's look (the default
.B deadd
preset: a black card at 0.8 opacity, no frame, the shadow left to the compositor) with dunst's
rule engine and command line control.
.PP
Replacing a notification by id keeps the id; the
.B x\-dunst\-stack\-tag
and
.B x\-canonical\-private\-synchronous
hints replace the previous notification with the same app and tag. The
.B value
hint draws a progress bar, actions become buttons, and a notification under the pointer does not
expire. Summary and body take Pango markup.
.PP
Every event (shown, replaced, waiting, suppressed, expired, dismissed, closed, action, pause,
reload) is written to standard error as an aligned line colored by urgency and event, or as JSON
lines, and broadcast on D\-Bus for
.BR "notifyd ctl watch" .
.PP
Every command takes
.BR \-h / \-\-help ,
except
.BR send ,
where
.B \-h
is
.B \-\-hint
as in
.BR notify\-send (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS daemon
Run the daemon in the foreground. It reloads its config when the file changes, on SIGHUP, or on
.BR "notifyd ctl reload" ;
a broken file is reported and the previous config kept.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIpath\fR"
Config file (default
.IR ~/.config/notifyd/config.yaml ).
.TP
.BR \-\-renderer " gtk|none"
.B none
draws nothing and only logs, for headless use and debugging.
.TP
.B \-\-replace
Take the bus name from the daemon that owns it (if it allows replacement). Without it, notifyd
exits with status 1 and names the daemon that owns the name.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-format " pretty|json"
Event log format (default: the config's
.BR log.format ,
pretty).
.TP
.BR \-\-color " auto|always|never"
Color the log; auto colors a terminal unless
.B NO_COLOR
is set.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log debug events too.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Log only warnings and errors.
.SS send
Send a notification through whichever daemon owns the notification name, with
.BR notify\-send (1)'s
flags and some of notify\-send.py's. With actions it waits and prints the key of the action chosen.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-app\-name " \fIname\fR"
The sending application; rules match on it.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-urgency " low|normal|critical"
Urgency.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-expire\-time " \fIms\fR"
How long to show it; 0 until closed. A rule's timeout wins over it.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-icon " \fIicon\fR"
App icon: an icon name or a path.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-category " \fItype\fR"
The category hint, e.g. email.arrived.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-hint " \fItype\fB:\fIname\fB:\fIvalue\fR"
An extra hint; type is int, double, string, byte or boolean. Repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-action " [\fIname\fB=\fR]\fItext\fR"
A button (also
.IB name : text\fR);
waits and prints the name chosen. Repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-replace\-id " \fIid\fR"
Replace notification
.IR id .
.TP
.BR \-\-replace\-name ", " \-\-replaces\-process " \fIname\fR"
Replace the last notification sent with this
.IR name ;
ids are kept in
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/notifyd/send\-ids.json .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print\-id
Print the notification id.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-transient
Keep it out of history.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wait
Wait until it is closed.
.TP
.BR \-\-tag " \fItag\fR"
Stack tag: replaces the last notification with this app and tag.
.TP
.BR \-\-image " \fIpath\fR"
A picture shown in the notification (sent as a file:// image\-path hint).
.TP
.BR \-\-progress " \fIn\fR"
A progress bar at
.I n
percent.
.TP
.BR \-\-close " \fIid\fR"
Close notification
.I id
and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show help.
.SS ctl
Control the running daemon over its
.B io.github.njhoffman.Notifyd
interface.
.TP
.B status
Paused state, how many are shown, waiting and held back, the preset and the config file.
.TP
.BR list " [\fB\-\-json\fR | \fB\-\-ids\fR]"
Open notifications: on screen (newest first), waiting for room, held back by pause.
.B \-\-ids
prints the id, a tab, the app and the summary, for scripts and completion.
.TP
.BR history " [\fB\-n\fR \fIn\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]"
The last
.I n
closed notifications (default 20, 0 for all), oldest first.
.TP
.BR pop " [\fIid\fR]"
Show a closed notification again: the last one in the history, or
.IR id .
.TP
.BI close " id"
Close a notification.
.TP
.BI action " id \fR[\fIkey\fR]"
Invoke an action: the key given, else the default action, else the first one.
.TP
.B close\-all
Close everything shown or waiting.
.TP
.BR pause ", " resume ", " toggle
Hold back all but critical notifications; resume shows what was held back.
.TP
.BR mode " [\fIname\fR]"
Show the mode, or set it. Rules match on it with
.BR "match: {mode: \fIname\fB}" ,
e.g. to suppress all but critical notifications in a
.B dnd
mode; the default mode is
.BR normal .
.TP
.B reload
Reload the config file; exits 1 with the error when it is broken.
.TP
.BI preset " name"
Switch the preset until the next reload.
.TP
.BR preview " [\fIpreset\fR]"
Show sample notifications (low, song with tags, volume bar, actions, critical) in a preset.
.TP
.BR watch " [\fB\-\-json\fR]"
Follow the daemon's event log.
.SS presets
List the presets with their descriptions.
.B \-\-pick
chooses one in
.BR fzf (1),
previewing each as the cursor moves and switching to it on enter;
.B \-\-names
prints the names only.
.SS import
.B notifyd import dunst
converts
.I ~/.config/dunst/dunstrc
(or
.BR \-\-rc ):
geometry, font, frame, urgency colors (with its transparency) and timeouts, idle threshold, mouse
buttons, and its rule sections (globs become regexes; skip_display, history_ignore, script,
new_icon, set_stack_tag and colors carry over), on top of the
.B dunst
preset.
.PP
.B notifyd import deadd
converts
.I ~/.config/deadd/deadd.yml
(or
.BR \-\-yml )
and the
.I deadd.css
next to it (or
.BR \-\-css )
and prints the config, or writes it with
.BR \-o / \-\-output
.I path
(\fB\-o config\fR for the default config file;
.B \-\-force
overwrites). Style values that equal the deadd preset are left out; notes on what has no
equivalent go to standard error.
.SS check
Validate the config. Exits 1 when there are warnings, 2 on errors.
.SS rules
Show which rules match a notification and what it would get:
.BR \-\-app ,
.BR \-\-summary ,
.BR \-\-body ,
.BR \-\-urgency " low|normal|critical,"
.BI \-\-timeout " ms"
(what the sender asks for) and
.BI \-\-hint " name\fB=\fIvalue"
(repeatable), plus
.BR \-c / \-\-config .
.SS completion
Print a completion script for
.BR zsh ,
.B bash
or
.BR fish .
Preset names complete live from the installed presets.
.SS help, version
.B notifyd help
.RI [ command ...]
prints the help of notifyd or a command (e.g.
.BR "notifyd help ctl history" );
.BR "notifyd version" ,
.B \-V
and
.B \-\-version
print the version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
YAML; every key is optional and an empty file gives the deadd look. The main keys:
.BR preset ,
.B style
(overrides of the preset's keys),
.BR width ,
.B timeout
(8000, 8s, 1500ms, 2m or never),
.BR timeout\-critical ,
.BR max\-visible ,
.B stack\-duplicates
(an identical notification replaces the open one and is counted),
.BR position.anchor / margin / gap / follow / monitor ,
.BR icon.size / name ,
.BR image.size / path / margin\-right ,
.BR body.max\-lines ,
.B markup
(full, strip, plain),
.BR hide ,
.BR class ,
.BR skip ,
.B sound
(a file or sound name; false silences),
.B buttons
(a list of
.BR "{label: \fItext\fB, run: \fIcommand\fB}" ),
.B run
(a command for each match),
.B idle\-threshold
(no expiry while the user is away that long),
.BR history.size / keep / persist ,
.BR log.format / color / level / file ,
.B click.left / middle / right
and
.BR rules .
.PP
A rule is a
.B match
plus any of those keys, applied in order to the notifications it matches:
.PP
.RS
.nf
rules:
  \- name: songs
    match: { app: [musicman, MPD, Spotify] }
    timeout: 12s
    hide: [app\-icon, app\-name]
  \- match: { summary: \(aq/(?P<pct>\ed+)% battery/i\(aq }
    urgency: critical
    summary: \(aqBattery at {pct}%\(aq
.fi
.RE
.PP
Match fields are app, summary, body, icon, category, desktop\-entry, stack\-tag, urgency, mode and
.BI hint: " {name: value}" ;
a value is an exact string, a
.BI / regex /
(with
.B i
to ignore case) or a list. Rules can also rewrite summary, body and app (templates with the
regex's named groups), urgency and stack\-tag. A rule's timeout wins over the sender's.
.PP
Presets are YAML files with a
.B style
mapping: colors, radius, border, padding, fonts per part (title, body, appname, time), urgency
colors, progress bar, buttons, raw CSS, and named
.B classes
that notification text can use as
.BR "<span class=\(dqaccent\(dq>" .
Bundled: deadd, dunst, minimal, card, tokyonight, high\-contrast.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/notifyd/config.yaml
The config.
.TP
.I ~/.config/notifyd/presets/*.yaml
Your presets; they shadow bundled ones of the same name.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/notifyd/history.jsonl
History kept across restarts (with
.BR history.persist ,
the default).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/notifyd/state.json
The mode, kept across restarts.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/notifyd/send\-ids.json
Ids for
.BR "notifyd send \-\-replace\-name" .
.PP
Commands from
.B run
and
.B buttons
run with
.BR sh (1)
in the background, with the notification as
.BR NOTIFYD_ID ,
.BR NOTIFYD_APP ,
.BR NOTIFYD_SUMMARY ,
.BR NOTIFYD_BODY ,
.BR NOTIFYD_URGENCY ,
.BR NOTIFYD_CATEGORY ,
.BR NOTIFYD_ICON ,
.B NOTIFYD_STACK_TAG
and
.B NOTIFYD_RULES
in the environment and as JSON on standard input.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the config directory is (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
No colors in the log or in
.BR "ctl watch" / history .
.TP
.BR DISPLAY ", " DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
The X display to draw on and the session bus.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the config.
.TP
.BR SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Close all notifications and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when the daemon cannot own the bus name or draw, a ctl command fails, or
.B check
finds warnings; 2 for usage and config errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
notifyd daemon \-\-replace
notifyd send \-a backdrop \-\-image ~/pic.jpg \(aqNew wallpaper\(aq \(aq<i>ocean</i>\(aq
notifyd send \-\-tag volume \-\-progress 60 \-a Volume \(aqVolume 60%\(aq
notifyd send \-A \(aqchange=Change layout\(aq \(aqMonitors changed\(aq
notifyd ctl watch
notifyd presets \-\-pick
notifyd import deadd \-o config
notifyd import dunst > dunst\-converted.yaml
notifyd ctl pop
notifyd completion zsh > ~/.local/share/zsh/site-functions/_notifyd
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notify\-send (1),
.BR dunst (1),
.BR picom (1),
.BR fzf (1).
The full config reference is
.I docs/config.md
in the source tree.
